msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Max Auto-tune Example\n"
"\n"
"This example demonstrates how to use the `max_autotune` parameter in `torch.compile` to automatically search for optimal configurations, thereby improving model performance. By setting `mode=\"max-autotune\"`, PyTorch will automatically tune the kernel to achieve the best performance on the current hardware.\n"
"\n"
"## Key Points\n"
"\n"
"- `torch.compile` is a tool provided by PyTorch for accelerating model inference and training.\n"
"- The `max_autotune` mode will automatically search for the optimal kernel configuration, which may increase compilation time but can bring performance improvements.\n"
"- This example shows how to use `max_autotune` to optimize a simple model.\n"
"\n"
"## Code Example\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch.nn as nn\n"
"import torch.optim as optim\n"
"\n"
"# Define a simple model\n"
"class SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super(SimpleModel, self).__init__()\n"
"        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(784, 256)\n"
"        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(256, 10)\n"
"\n"
"    def forward(self, x):\n"
"        x = torch.relu(self.fc1(x))\n"
"        x = self.fc2(x)\n"
"        return x\n"
"\n"
"# Create model and input\n"
"model = SimpleModel()\n"
"input_tensor = torch.randn(64, 784)\n"
"\n"
"# Use torch.compile with max_autotune mode\n"
"optimized_model = torch.compile(model, mode=\"max-autotune\")\n"
"\n"
"# Forward pass\n"
"output = optimized_model(input_tensor)\n"
"print(output.shape)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Explanation\n"
"\n"
"1. **Model Definition**: We define a simple two-layer fully connected neural network.\n"
"2. **Model Compilation**: Use `torch.compile` and set `mode=\"max-autotune\"` to enable automatic tuning.\n"
"3. **Forward Pass**: Perform a forward pass on the compiled model and print the output shape.\n"
"\n"
"## Notes\n"
"\n"
"- The `max_autotune` mode may significantly increase compilation time, especially for complex models.\n"
"- On some hardware, the performance improvement may not be obvious, so it is recommended to test on the actual deployment hardware.\n"
"- If you encounter issues during compilation, you can try using the default mode or other modes (such as `reduce-overhead`).\n"

msgid "max_autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "max_autotune usage example"

msgid "`max_autotune` 是 Triton-Ascend 提供的增强自动调优装饰器，旨在简化多参数调优的代码编写。与社区版 `autotune` 要求用户手动枚举所有 `triton.Config` 不同，`max_autotune` 允许用户仅提供少量基础配置（如分块大小），并自动将相关的编译器选项（如 `num_stages`、`enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance` 等）纳入最优组合的搜索空间。用户也可以通过参数列表显式控制搜索范围。"
msgstr "`max_autotune` is an enhanced auto-tuning decorator provided by Triton-Ascend, designed to simplify the code writing for multi-parameter tuning. Unlike the community version of `autotune`, which requires users to manually enumerate all `triton.Config` instances, `max_autotune` allows users to provide only a few basic configurations (such as block sizes) and automatically includes related compiler options (such as `num_stages`, `enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance`, etc.) in the search space for the optimal combination. Users can also explicitly control the search scope through a parameter list."

msgid "**适用场景**：Ascend NPU 上的 `cube`、`mix`、`vector` 算子，尤其适合需要同时调整多个硬件相关参数的场景。"
msgstr "**Applicable Scenarios**: `cube`, `mix`, and `vector` operators on Ascend NPU, especially suitable for scenarios where multiple hardware-related parameters need to be adjusted simultaneously."

msgid "基本使用示例"
msgstr "Basic usage example"

msgid "以下示例演示了使用 `max_autotune` 对一个简单的向量加法 kernel 进行自动调优。与社区版 `autotune` 相比，`max_autotune` 还会自动将不同的编译器选项纳入调优空间，无需用户手动指定。"
msgstr "The following example demonstrates using `max_autotune` to automatically tune a simple vector addition kernel. Compared to the community edition's `autotune`, `max_autotune` also automatically includes different compiler options in the tuning space, without requiring users to specify them manually."

msgid "进阶使用：精确控制调优参数"
msgstr "Advanced Usage: Precisely Controlling Tuning Parameters"

msgid "用户可以通过 **tuning_params 显式指定需要调优的编译器选项及其取值列表；未指定的参数会使用内置默认值。以下示例展示了如何对多个参数进行组合搜索。"
msgstr "Users can explicitly specify the compiler options to be tuned and their value lists via **tuning_params**; unspecified parameters will use built-in default values. The following example demonstrates how to perform a combined search over multiple parameters."
